1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,324
Three questions.

2
00:00:01,544 --> 00:00:02,792
Can you get all three?

3
00:00:03,012 --> 00:00:03,978
Morning quiz!

4
00:00:04,698 --> 00:00:05,619
Question one.

5
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:06,630
sum takes any

6
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:07,543
number of ints.

7
00:00:07,763 --> 00:00:09,077
We call it with zero,

8
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:10,454
one and three numbers.

9
00:00:10,674 --> 00:00:11,587
What prints?

10
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:12,904
Pause and answer.

11
00:00:13,624 --> 00:00:14,918
Zero, five, six.

12
00:00:15,138 --> 00:00:16,131
The dots turn the

13
00:00:16,131 --> 00:00:17,475
arguments into a slice.

14
00:00:17,695 --> 00:00:19,236
With no arguments, the

15
00:00:19,236 --> 00:00:20,497
slice is empty, so

16
00:00:20,497 --> 00:00:21,968
the total stays zero.

17
00:00:22,688 --> 00:00:23,718
Question two.

18
00:00:23,938 --> 00:00:25,231
Look at the plan column.

19
00:00:25,451 --> 00:00:26,740
Is it a number, text,

20
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,091
a date, or a category?

21
00:00:28,311 --> 00:00:29,408
Pause and answer.

22
00:00:30,128 --> 00:00:30,833
Category.

23
00:00:31,053 --> 00:00:32,428
Plan is a small set

24
00:00:32,428 --> 00:00:34,092
of labels, Free or Pro.

25
00:00:34,312 --> 00:00:35,610
So you count per plan.

26
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:37,457
Three users are on Pro.

27
00:00:38,177 --> 00:00:39,291
Interview question.

28
00:00:39,511 --> 00:00:40,745
We use colon equals

29
00:00:40,745 --> 00:00:42,108
outside any function.

30
00:00:42,328 --> 00:00:43,494
Does it compile, or

31
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:44,414
is it an error?

32
00:00:44,634 --> 00:00:45,731
Pause and answer.

33
00:00:46,451 --> 00:00:46,998
Error!

34
00:00:47,218 --> 00:00:48,709
Colon equals works only

35
00:00:48,709 --> 00:00:49,876
inside a function.

36
00:00:50,096 --> 00:00:51,418
Outside, write var

37
00:00:51,418 --> 00:00:52,446
x equals five.

38
00:00:52,666 --> 00:00:53,891
How many did you get?

39
00:00:54,111 --> 00:00:55,259
One, two or three?

40
00:00:55,479 --> 00:00:56,958
Follow CareerWithCode!

